@tradition four-weeks-aboard
// Four weeks aboard: your fourth Friday (day 26). At Works Friday tea (same deck and time as the weekly works-tea,
// which it replaces that Friday) the Works team has a cake for you, and Calder says a few words. The galley bakes it
// (cake: yes) and sends it to the Works tea corner, not the mess: plans/trad-notes-seasons.md.
k: 482
title: Four weeks aboard
when: arrival friday 4
at: 18:40-19:30
min: 20
prio: 2
early: 5
where: 5 room Tea corner: lounge-seat
where: 5 room Works bay: work:works, free
where: 5 room Machine shop: work:works, free
where: 5 room Main storage: work:works, free
hold: 1
who: calder always, torres-zeke always, pell always, works 90%, friends-of-host 40%
anim: calder talk, everyone drink
host: calder
from: The Works team
cake: yes

== mail
- Friday tea tomorrow, {time}, is a special one: four weeks aboard. Someone in Works has asked the galley for a cake. We're not saying who.

== ask
- Friday tea tonight. Don't eat too much at dinner.   #funny
- Four weeks! That calls for cake. Works tea corner, after dinner.
- You've been here a month. I can't believe it.   #warm

== here
- Four weeks, and the board's never been cleaner.
- Cut it yourself. The new hand cuts the four-week cake. It's the rule.   #funny
- You're one of us now. You were before, but now there's cake.   #warm

== thanks
- The Works team has a cake for your four weeks aboard. Calder says a few words, and they're kind ones.   #warm

== chatter
- Four weeks for the new hand. They had a cake at Friday tea.
- The four-week cake is a Works thing. The Chief started it, years ago.
